      "text": "The script builds SMB as the average of three size factors, one from each 2x3 sort (B/M, OP, Inv). Each size factor is the equal-weighted average of the three small value-weighted portfolios minus the equal-weighted average of the three big ones. Output covers 1963-07 onward, where all three sorts are available.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nFILES = [\n    \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\",          # size x B/M\n    \"6_Portfolios_ME_OP_2x3.csv\",    # size x OP\n    \"6_Portfolios_ME_INV_2x3.csv\",   # size x Inv\n]\nMISSING = (-99.99, -999.0)\n\n\ndef read_vw_monthly(path):\n    \"\"\"Parse the 'Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly' block of a Ken French file.\n    Returns a DataFrame indexed by YYYYMM int with 6 columns in file order:\n    SMALL Lo, ME1 mid, SMALL Hi, BIG Lo, ME2 mid, BIG Hi.\"\"\"\n    with open(path, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        low = line.lower()\n        if \"value weighted returns\" in low and \"monthly\" in low:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        start = -1  # fallback: scan whole file\n\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        if parts and re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]) and len(parts) >= 7:\n            vals = []\n            for p in parts[1:7]:\n                try:\n                    v = float(p)\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if any(np.isclose(v, m) for m in MISSING):\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            rows.append([int(parts[0])] + vals)\n            started = True\n        elif started:\n            break  # end of the monthly block\n\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"date\"] + list(range(6)))\n    df = df.set_index(\"date\").sort_index()\n    return df\n\n\ndef size_factor_from_file(path):\n    d = read_vw_monthly(path)\n    small = d[[0, 1, 2]].mean(axis=1, skipna=False)  # avg of 3 small portfolios\n    big = d[[3, 4, 5]].mean(axis=1, skipna=False)    # avg of 3 big portfolios\n    return small - big\n\n\ndef main():\n    series = [size_factor_from_file(f) for f in FILES]\n    # Align on months where all three sorts are available\n    combined = pd.concat(series, axis=1, join=\"inner\").dropna()\n    smb = combined.mean(axis=1)  # SMB = (SMB_BM + SMB_OP + SMB_INV) / 3\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame({\n        \"date\": smb.index.astype(int),\n        \"value\": smb.values.astype(float),\n    })\n    out = out.sort_values(\"date\").reset_index(drop=True)\n    out.to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n**Method notes**\n\n- **Parsing:** Each file's \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" block is read until the first non-data line. Missing codes (-99.99, -999) become NaN.\n- **Per-sort size factor:** For each 2x3 sort, the small leg is the simple average of the three small portfolios (Lo, mid, Hi), and the big leg is the average of the three big portfolios. The size factor is small minus big.\n- **Combined SMB:** The 5-factor SMB is the simple average of the three size factors (B/M, OP, Inv). Only months where all three are available are kept, so the series starts in July 1963 (the OP and Inv files start there).\n- **Units:** Values stay in percent, as in the inputs.",
